---
title: "The end of a stopped run does not free the run after it"
---
sequenceDiagram
  participant You as You
  participant G as Busy registry
  participant R1 as Run 1
  participant R2 as Run 2
  participant J1 as Job 1
  participant J2 as Job 2
  participant L as LLM
  You->>G: start Autoplay
  Note over G: Run 1 holds the Game
  R1->>G: accept my next Job
  G-->>R1: accepted: Job 1 starts
  J1->>G: set the step
  J1->>L: narrator call
  You->>G: Stop
  Note over G: the holder goes, and its work is cut off
  You->>G: start Autoplay
  Note over G: Run 2 holds the Game
  L-->>J1: the Narration
  J1-xG: save the text: refused, the holder is not Job 1
  Note over J1: Job 1 ends and writes nothing more
  Note over R1: its Job ended, so the run ends
  R1->>G: end the run
  Note over G: the holder is the next run, so it stays
  R2->>G: accept my next Job
  G-->>R2: accepted: Job 2 starts
